WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.826 --> 00:00:13.447
was movie day at Kids Central.

2
00:00:14.827 --> 00:00:16.508
The kids had just watched a cartoon.

3
00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:20.691
When it was over, Miss Shelly turned on the lights.

4
00:00:20.711 --> 00:00:25.693
"I love cartoons, especially space adventures," Jason said.

5
00:00:25.713 --> 00:00:29.936
"Miss Shelly, can we draw pictures from the movie?"

6
00:00:31.092 --> 00:00:34.035
"Jason is really good at drawing," Ethan said.

7
00:00:34.055 --> 00:00:38.378
"My mom just signed me up for art lessons," Jason said.

8
00:00:38.398 --> 00:00:40.460
"My first lesson is today."

9
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.842
"Fun!" Izzie said.

10
00:00:43.763 --> 00:00:45.064
Jason looked unsure.

11
00:00:45.084 --> 00:00:48.026
"I hope the teacher doesn't tell me what to draw.

12
00:00:48.046 --> 00:00:50.848
I like drawing my own stuff."

13
00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:56.934
"Well, I think you'll like today's drawing activity, Jason," Miss Shelly said.

14
00:00:56.954 --> 00:00:59.596
"We're going to make flip books.

15
00:01:00.404 --> 00:01:03.425
We'll draw cartoons and turn them into movies."

16
00:01:03.445 --> 00:01:06.166
"That's called animation!"

17
00:01:06.447 --> 00:01:07.227
Jason said.

18
00:01:07.247 --> 00:01:11.749
"Right!" Miss Shelly smiled and held up a small booklet.

19
00:01:11.769 --> 00:01:13.810
"This is my flip book.

20
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.051
I made a movie with a dancing dot.

21
00:01:17.551 --> 00:01:20.532
Watch." Miss Shelly flipped the pages of her book.

22
00:01:21.653 --> 00:01:23.714
A dot with feet danced across the paper.

23
00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:29.236
"It looks like that dot is really moving," Izzie said.

24
00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:33.355
Miss Shelly handed out three sheets of paper to everyone.

25
00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:38.399
"Stack the sheets of paper and fold them in half," she said.

26
00:01:38.419 --> 00:01:42.883
"Cut along the fold so you get two stacks of paper.

27
00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.848
Next fold each stack in half lengthwise.

28
00:01:49.269 --> 00:01:55.394
Cut each fold and now you'll have—" "Twelve strips," Jason said.

29
00:01:55.415 --> 00:02:00.943
"Yep. Now stack the strips and fold that stack in half."

30
00:02:02.544 --> 00:02:06.026
"Now we staple the pages on the folded side, right?"

31
00:02:06.387 --> 00:02:07.087
Ethan asked.

32
00:02:07.107 --> 00:02:09.829
"That makes a booklet with 24 pages."

33
00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:16.194
"Right. After that, I'll show you how to start drawing," Miss Shelly said.

34
00:02:16.214 --> 00:02:20.337
"Can I make a basketball go into a hoop?"

35
00:02:20.677 --> 00:02:21.457
Bobby asked.

36
00:02:21.477 --> 00:02:24.800
"Great idea," Miss Shelly said.

37
00:02:25.864 --> 00:02:28.645
"I'm going to draw a boy surfing," Ethan said.

38
00:02:29.486 --> 00:02:30.506
Jason smiled.

39
00:02:30.806 --> 00:02:32.147
He knew what he wanted to draw.

40
00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:38.029
"Turn to the last page of your flip book," Miss Shelly said.

41
00:02:38.049 --> 00:02:40.770
"Your first drawing goes here."

42
00:02:41.511 --> 00:02:43.391
She pointed to the lower part of the page.

43
00:02:44.672 --> 00:02:45.872
Everyone started drawing.

44
00:02:45.892 --> 00:02:50.474
"I'm making someone jumping rope," said Nina.

45
00:02:50.494 --> 00:02:54.216
"Turn to the next page," Miss Shelly said.

46
00:02:54.772 --> 00:02:56.853
"Can you see your drawing through the paper?"

47
00:02:57.833 --> 00:02:58.733
Everyone nodded.

48
00:02:58.753 --> 00:03:04.135
"Trace that drawing—except for the part that is going to move.

49
00:03:04.935 --> 00:03:06.375
You'll draw that part again.

50
00:03:07.195 --> 00:03:10.997
But you'll draw it in a different place," Miss Shelly explained.

51
00:03:11.017 --> 00:03:13.637
"I get it," Jason said.

52
00:03:13.657 --> 00:03:16.338
"Each page shows the same picture.

53
00:03:17.118 --> 00:03:20.159
But something in the picture has moved just a little bit."

54
00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:23.400
"Yep!" Miss Shelly said.

55
00:03:23.964 --> 00:03:25.925
"Start making animations, kids!"

56
00:03:27.005 --> 00:03:30.647
Page by page, Bobby drew the basketball closer to the hoop.

57
00:03:34.229 --> 00:03:36.550
Then he flipped the pages from the back to the front.

58
00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:41.932
"Yes! The basketball flies into the hoop!"

59
00:03:42.872 --> 00:03:44.213
Izzie tried hers next.

60
00:03:44.533 --> 00:03:47.034
Her frog, Gurpy, hopped across the page.

61
00:03:48.075 --> 00:03:50.796
"Look at Ethan's movie," Nina said.

62
00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.401
"He made a shark appear behind the surfer!"

63
00:03:56.581 --> 00:03:58.122
Jason held up his flip book.

64
00:03:58.762 --> 00:03:59.982
He flipped through the pages.

65
00:04:00.803 --> 00:04:01.943
A spaceship appeared.

66
00:04:02.783 --> 00:04:05.224
It sucked a dog into the ship and flew away.

67
00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:09.385
"That's the best one!"

68
00:04:09.645 --> 00:04:10.485
Bobby cried.

69
00:04:10.505 --> 00:04:12.566
"I want to make more movies."

70
00:04:12.966 --> 00:04:13.966
Jason grinned.

71
00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:18.708
"Hey! Maybe my new drawing teacher can give me some tips today."
